Article 18 (Request for Reissuance of International Money Order Certificate)
(1) In any of the following cases, the payee shall submit an International Money Order Certificate Reissuance Request to a post office:
1. Where the validity period of the international money order certificate has expired;
2. Where the international money order certificate has been lost;
3. Where the international money order certificate has been soiled or damaged so that the name of the issuing or receiving post office, issue number or symbol number, amount payable, or address or name of the payee is unclear.
(2) Where reissuance is requested for a reason under paragraph (1) 1 or 3, the relevant international money order certificate shall be attached to the reissuance request.
